title: authority_information
---
<<present_speaker "npc_authority_information">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_information_met") == "satisfied">>
    Ottilie: Information. How can I help?
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_information_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "authority_information_met" true>>
    Ottilie: Welcome to the Concourse. Information. How can I direct you?
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<jump authority_information__topics>>
===

title: authority_information__topics
---
-> Where can I go from here?
    Ottilie: The terminal lists public addresses. For an unlisted one, ask the office that runs that gate.
    Ottilie: Keep LEGAL written down. It is this gate, and every terminal lists it.
    Ottilie: Our terminal also posts a way back to the public hub. If you know another address, you can dial it yourself.
    <<jump authority_information__topics>>
-> Where am I?
    Ottilie: The Concourse, seat of the Gate Authority. This gate is LEGAL.
    Ottilie: Authority Plaza is east. Lost Baggage is down through the grate. Mind the claw.
    <<jump authority_information__topics>>
-> What is the Iron Bastion?
    Ottilie: The military tower. The General has his office there; ask him if you need clearance for the military annex. We handle the civilian ring here.
    <<jump authority_information__topics>>
-> Where can I recover from a crossing?
    Ottilie: Rest here in the Concourse. Some need a few minutes, some most of the day. If you are still ill after the others recover, ask a member of staff.
    <<jump authority_information__topics>>
-> Who works out when the gates are open?
    Ottilie: The timetable office. We asked them for more evening passenger slots because people were sleeping on the benches here.
    Ottilie: They sent me a letter from a station freight clerk asking for one of his slots back. I have to find out how many passengers we actually send on Thursdays.
    <<jump authority_information__topics>>
-> ‹go›
===
title: authority_baggage
---
<<present_speaker "npc_authority_baggage">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_baggage_met") == "satisfied">>
    Bertram: Still no ticket? Then still no bag.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_baggage_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "authority_baggage_met" true>>
    Bertram: Lost Baggage. Ticket?
    Bertram: No ticket. Course not. Nobody who comes down here has a ticket. That's why they come down here.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
-> What happens to a bag in a gate?
    Bertram: Depends on the gate. A holdall went through to the dinosaurs and came back a nest. Egg and all. It's on the belt.
    Bertram: One came back from the hill country a cloud. It's on the shelf. Mind it doesn't rain on you.
-> Why "declare any sentience"?
    Bertram: Organic travellers' bags. Leather remembers it was a cow. Now and then it goes home.
-> ‹go›
===
title: authority_gatekeeper
---
<<present_speaker "npc_authority_gatekeeper">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_gatekeeper_met") == "satisfied">>
    Imre: Morning. Keep the gate clear, please.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_gatekeeper_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "authority_gatekeeper_met" true>>
    Imre: Gatekeeper Imre, Gate Authority. Papers?
    Imre: If you've just arrived, keep to this side while I clear the landing area.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<jump authority_gatekeeper__topics>>
===

title: authority_gatekeeper__topics
---
-> What does the Authority do?
    Imre: We survey rings, maintain terminals, and keep records of crossings at our posts. Anybody can dial a working gate if they know the address.
    Imre: People tend to come to us when they need the address, or when something breaks.
    <<jump authority_gatekeeper__topics>>
-> Who were you at war with?
    Imre: The regime that runs Castle Godwin. The last dispatch we had said we'd held our lines. Neither side got much farther than that.
    Imre: We have an armistice. I hope it lasts.
    <<jump authority_gatekeeper__topics>>
-> What is the clock for?
    Imre: Every licensed gate keeps its time by that clock. It is never wrong.
    Imre: Occasionally it is corrected.
    <<jump authority_gatekeeper__topics>>
-> Does the military use this gate?
    Imre: Sometimes. Their annex has its own checkpoint. If they want to bring a squad through here, I ask them to wait until the civilians are clear.
    <<jump authority_gatekeeper__topics>>
-> Who can dial a military gate?
    Imre: Anybody who has its address. Getting past the sentry when you arrive is another question.
    <<jump authority_gatekeeper__topics>>
-> ‹go›
===
title: authority_registrar
---
<<present_speaker "npc_authority_registrar">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_registrar_met") == "satisfied">>
    Registrar: Now serving four thousand and ninety-six. You are sixty-five thousand, five hundred and thirty-seven.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "authority_registrar_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "authority_registrar_met" true>>
    Registrar: Number?
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<jump authority_registrar__topics>>
===

title: authority_registrar__topics
---
-> What if I don't have a number?
    Registrar: Then you were never in the queue. Then you were never here. That's quicker for both of us.
    <<jump authority_registrar__topics>>
-> What is this place?
    Registrar: The Manifest Office. We receive manifests from the staffed gates. If an office reports the same passenger twice, we have to reconcile the entries.
    Registrar: And if a director sends a correction, we file the corrected record. No, you cannot see the original.
    <<jump authority_registrar__topics>>
-> Can you check whether I am on the manifest?
    Registrar: Let me see. Nothing under that name in the copy I have.
    Registrar: Bring me the receipt from your last crossing. I can ask that office for its record.
    <<jump authority_registrar__topics>>
-> Do you keep records for the military?
    Registrar: Ask the Iron Bastion for their annex logs. They send me summaries. They do not send them often enough.
    Registrar: Brandt keeps sending me copies of a summary I already have. I am asking for the sheet that tells me who arrived.
    <<jump authority_registrar__topics>>
-> ‹go›
===
